---
title: "Plant Propagation (Fall)"
code: "HRT-115"
category: "horticulture"
credits: "3"
prerequisites: []
corequisites: []
---

Teaches principles and practices of plant propagation. Examines commercial and home practices. Provides experience in techniques using seed-spores, cuttings, grafting, budding, layering and division. Lecture 2 hours. Laboratory 2 hours. Total 4 hours per week. Additional course fee applies.
